{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018yevdovb2xoFcUDngRZdsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier scenario. Let me identify which experiments are still in \"planned\" status:\n\n1. plan_001 - real_data_dif_mmlu - status: planned\n2. plan_002 - rl_robustness_validation - status: planned\n3. plan_003a - constat_perturbation_eval - status: planned\n4. plan_003b - dvd_generation_variance_eval - status: planned\n5. plan_003c - ensemble_fusion - status: planned\n\n\n6. plan_004 - cross_benchmark_gsm8k - status: planned (though it's marked as DONE in the registry)\n7. plan_005 - bifactor_irt_equating_pilot - status: planned\n8. plan_006 - item_generation_calibration - status: planned\n9. plan_007 - cumulative_bayesian_dif - status: planned\n10. plan_008 - graceful_degradation_analysis - status: planned\n11. plan_009 - item_focused_trees - status: planned\n12. plan_010 - architecture_stratified_dif - status: planned (though it's mentioned as \"executing\" in the claims)\n13. plan_011 - semi_synthetic_contamination - status: planned (but registry shows DONE)\n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy here. The experiment_plan lists everything as \"planned,\" but the registry already has results for several of these. The user is asking for predictions on the planned experiments, so I need to identify which ones are actually still pending versus already completed. Looking at what's in the registry, plan_001, plan_004, plan_011 through plan_014, plan_016, and plan_017 are already done, while plan_015 was killed. The truly pending ones appear to be plan_002, plan_003a through plan_003c, plan_005, plan_006, and a few others that haven't been executed yet.\n\nFor the worst-case tier scenario, I'm working with the assumption that architecture stratification reveals most temporal DIF is actually population heterogeneity artifact, which fundamentally undermines the IRT model assumptions. I need to generate detailed predictions for all the planned experiments under this pessimistic outcome.\n\nLooking at the key metrics ranges for this tier—decoder-only C percentage between 5-14%, RMSEA between 0.05-0.08%, CFI between 0.8-0.9%, and the partial correlations hovering near zero with high p-values—the pattern suggests the core claim about temporal DIF collapses, leaving only the meta-critique and semi-synthetic framework as viable contributions.\n\nNow I'm working through what each experiment would actually show under this worst-case scenario. Plan_001 would still produce its 31.3% C percentage because it uses the full population, but plan_010's architecture stratification would later expose this as an artifact. Plan_002 would reveal that DIF flags are inconsistent across different cohort compositions, making the AUROC comparison uninformative given the high false positive rate. Plan_003a would show ConStat detecting moderate issues, but the DIF comparison itself becomes compromised by DIF's fundamental misspecification. For plan_003b, I need to think through what the DVD generation variance would show under these conditions. the items being replaced were flagged by a flawed method. Plan 009 with item-focused trees might reveal the architecture confound more directly through continuous treatment analysis. Plan 010 is the critical worst-case test—architecture stratification shows decoder-only performance drops sharply to 5-14% with persistent IRT misfit. Plan 011 validates the semi-synthetic framework, which still produces positive signal injection effects despite high baseline false positives, making it valuable as infrastructure regardless of whether MH-DIF is the right detector. Now I'm writing the full YAML output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17325,"c